<title>CANADA: UGG details W. Canada wheat supply/disposition.</title>
<headline>UGG details W. Canada wheat supply/disposition.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Grain Growers on Wednesday detailed its estimate of supply and disposition of wheat in western Canada based on a farmer survey by United Grain Growers elevator managers between June 2 and 4.</p>
<p>			     WESTERN CANADA (in '000 tonnes)</p>
<p>	   Forecast 97/98    Forecast 96/97   Five-Yr-Avg</p>
<p>Supply</p>
<p>Open stks 10,228		 6,633		9,868</p>
<p>Output    27,104		30,495	     27,443</p>
<p>Imports	 20		   100		   19</p>
<p>Total     37,352		37,228	     37,330</p>
<p>Disposition</p>
<p>Exports   19,500		18,000	     20,152</p>
<p>Seed	 1,300		 1,300		1,194</p>
<p>Human Food 2,700		 2,700		2,581</p>
<p>Feed/Waste 4,300		 5,000		4,344</p>
<p>Total     27,800		27,000	     28,271</p>
<p>Carryout   9,552		10,228		9,059</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
